Day 1 — GCP Compute Engine (GCE): 
Scenario-Based DevOps Interview Questions

1️⃣ What is the difference between a zonal, regional, and global resource in GCP? Where does Compute Engine fit?

2️⃣ Your Compute Engine VM is experiencing high CPU usage. How would you troubleshoot and scale it without downtime?

3️⃣ Explain the difference between “Preemptible VMs” and “Standard VMs”. When would you use preemptible instances in DevOps pipelines?

4️⃣ You need to migrate 10 on-prem VMs to GCE. Which GCP service or approach would you use and why?

5️⃣ How do you restrict SSH access to Compute Engine VMs using IAM roles instead of static keys?

6️⃣ What is a startup script in GCE? Give an example of a DevOps use case where it saves deployment time.

7️⃣ A VM accidentally got deleted. How can you recover it or avoid such incidents in production?

8️⃣ Your application requires multiple disks with high IOPS. Which GCE disk types would you choose and why?

9️⃣ How do Instance Templates and Managed Instance Groups (MIGs) work together for autoscaling?

